module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorLeftUnitorSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealActionFactorization
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.QuasiCoherent.TildeTensorSections

/-!
# The action of the ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme, on sections

Let `X` be a scheme and `D ⊆ X` a closed subscheme with ideal sheaf `ℐ_D`. The action

`ℐ_D ⊗_{𝒪_X} G ⟶ G`

of `Stacks.Divisors.idealAction` has a sheafified tensor product as its source, so a statement
about it is not directly a statement about sections. This file removes the tensor product from
such statements: the action carries the image of a local pure tensor `r ⊗ s` to the scalar
multiple `ι(r) · s`, and a morphism out of the tensor product is determined by its values on
those images, so the vanishing

`ℐ_D · G ⟶ G ⟶ N` is zero

follows from a condition on sections alone.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.idealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection`: **the action on a local pure
  tensor is scalar multiplication** by the image of the first factor under the inclusion
  `ℐ_D ⟶ 𝒪_X`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.idealAction_comp_eq_zero`: **a morphism `h` out of `G` kills the image of the
  action of `ℐ_D` as soon as it kills the image of every local pure tensor.**

Together these are the shape in which the hypothesis of `Stacks.Divisors.twistedRetraction` —
the containment `ℐ_D · G ⊆ F`, spelled as `idealAction D G ≫ cokernel.π λ = 0` — becomes a
statement about sections: what has to be shown is that `ι(r) · s` is killed by `cokernel.π λ`
for every section `r` of `ℐ_D` and every section `s` of `G` over a common open. Vanishing of a
single section is local on that open, so this may then be checked over the opens of a covering;
on an open where `ℐ_D` is generated by one section `f`, `ι(r)` is a multiple of `f`
(`Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero`), so the condition becomes that `f · s`
lies in the image of `λ` on sections.

## Implementation notes

Everything is written at the ringed-space spelling `SheafOfModules (structureSheafRing
X.toRingedSpace)` of the category of `𝒪_X`-modules rather than at `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.
Modules`. The two are the same category — the sheaves of rings are equal by `rfl`, which is why
`Stacks.Divisors.idealAction` applies to an object of either — but the scalar action on the
sections of a sheaf of modules is found by instance search only at the first spelling, so a
statement mentioning `r • s` has to be phrased there. For the same reason the scalar is passed
through `Stacks.SheafOfModules.structureSection`, the ascription of a section of the monoidal
unit as a section of the structure sheaf.

The pure-tensor formula is the computation of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.denominatorIdealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection` for an arbitrary
ideal sheaf in place of the ideal of denominators of [Stacks, Tag 02P2]; both actions are the
functoriality of the sheaf tensor product applied to an ideal inclusion, followed by the left
unit constraint.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.SheafOfModules (structureSection)
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace (toTensorSheafSection tensorSheaf_hom_ext
  tensorSheafMap_app_toTensorSheafSection)
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (D : X.IdealSheafData)
  (G N : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace))

/-- **The action of the ideal sheaf of `D` on a local pure tensor is scalar multiplication.**
The scalar is the image of the first factor under the inclusion `ℐ_D ⟶ 𝒪_X`.

The action is the functoriality of the sheaf tensor product applied to that inclusion, followed
by the left unit constraint; the first step is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.tensorSheafMap_app_toTensorSheafSection` and the
second is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorProductLeftUnitor_hom_val_app_toTensorSheafSection`.

Unlike `Stacks.SheafOfModules.denominatorIdealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection`, which this
computation otherwise follows, those two steps do not meet by `rfl`.
`Stacks.Divisors.idealAction` tensors the inclusion through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.tensorRightMap`, which is `((- ⊗ -).map ι).app G`, while the
first lemma is stated at `CategoryTheory.Functor.uncurry`; the two differ by the factor
`(F.obj B).map (𝟙 G)`, which `huncurry` removes. `huncurry` is stated for an arbitrary sheaf of
rings on the site rather than for `X`'s own, because `rw` re-typechecks its goal at `implicit`
transparency, and there neither `X.sheaf` nor `⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩` is type-correct in this
position -- `TopCat.Sheaf` does not unfold at that transparency. -/
theorem idealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection (U : (Opens ↥(X : TopCat.{u}))ᵒᵖ)
    (r : (negativeTwist' D).val.obj U) (s : G.val.obj U) :
    ((idealAction D G).val.app U).hom
        (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (negativeTwist' D) G U
          (r ⊗ₜ[X.toRingedSpace.presheaf.obj U] s)) =
      structureSection X.toRingedSpace U (((idealSheafInclusion D).val.app U).hom r) • s := by
  have huncurry : ∀ (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥(X : TopCat.{u})) CommRingCat.{u})
      (A B Y : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R)) (f : A ⟶ B),
      (Functor.uncurry.obj (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} R)).map
          ((f, 𝟙 Y) : (A, Y) ⟶ (B, Y)) =
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} R).map f).app Y := by
    intro R A B Y f
    simp only [CategoryTheory.Functor.uncurry]
    rw [CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, Category.comp_id]
  have hmap := tensorSheafMap_app_toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (negativeTwist' D) G
    (SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace)) G
    (idealSheafInclusion D) (𝟙 G) U.unop r s
  have hbridge := (congrArg (fun morphism => (morphism.val.app U).hom
      (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (negativeTwist' D) G U
        (r ⊗ₜ[X.toRingedSpace.presheaf.obj U] s)))
      (huncurry _ _ _ G (idealSheafInclusion D)).symm).trans hmap
  exact (congrArg (fun z => ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.tensorProductLeftUnitor
        X.toRingedSpace.presheaf (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property
        G).hom.val.app U).hom z) hbridge).trans
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorProductLeftUnitor_hom_val_app_toTensorSheafSection
      X.toRingedSpace G U
      (structureSection X.toRingedSpace U (((idealSheafInclusion D).val.app U).hom r)) s)

/-- **A morphism out of `G` kills the image of the action of `ℐ_D` as soon as it kills every
section of the form `ι(r) · s`.**

A morphism out of the sheaf tensor product `ℐ_D ⊗_{𝒪_X} G` is determined by its values on the
images of local pure tensors
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.tensorSheaf_hom_ext`), and on such an image the
action is scalar multiplication by `ι(r)`. -/
theorem idealAction_comp_eq_zero {G' N' : X.Modules} (h : G' ⟶ N')
    (hz : ∀ (U : (Opens ↥(X : TopCat.{u}))ᵒᵖ) (r : (negativeTwist' D).val.obj U)
      (s : G'.val.obj U), (h.val.app U).hom (((idealAction D G').val.app U).hom
        (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (negativeTwist' D) G' U
          (r ⊗ₜ[X.toRingedSpace.presheaf.obj U] s))) = 0) :
    idealAction D G' ≫ h = 0 := by
  refine tensorSheaf_hom_ext (X := X.toRingedSpace) (F := negativeTwist' D) (G := G') (K := N')
    fun U r s => ?_
  have hcomp : ((idealAction D G' ≫ h).val.app U).hom
      (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (negativeTwist' D) G' U
        (r ⊗ₜ[X.toRingedSpace.presheaf.obj U] s)) =
      (h.val.app U).hom (((idealAction D G').val.app U).hom
        (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (negativeTwist' D) G' U
          (r ⊗ₜ[X.toRingedSpace.presheaf.obj U] s))) := rfl
  exact hcomp.trans (hz U r s)

end Stacks.Divisors

end
